<!--Post: 9832--><!--Time: 1109656869-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9832"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dz<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dz<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 10:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->i found on crime &amp; justice resource post something called RIVERVIEW ROUND-UP i dont know exactly what it is but it says there that he want to &#34;garden a lot&#34; i have not heard about what you say but i think that is probable right.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9832-->
<!--Post: 9885--><!--Time: 1109688798-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9885"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rev<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rev<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 6:53 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I saw a video &#40;don&#39;t remember where since there&#39;s so much to watch&#41; where LE was in his back yard pulling things out of the ground.  The only thing I could make out was a necklace. <BR> <BR>I&#39;ve heard from someone who knew his family that he had a shed in his backyard, and their theory is that most of it was in there. <BR> <BR>Dz, the Riverview Round-Up is like a survey from his 8th grade reunion asking the students what they had been doing since graduating from 8th grade.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9885-->
<!--Post: 9895--><!--Time: 1109695872-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9895"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 8:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rev it was the shot on CNN! Rader has a small shed attached to the back of his house, they were pulling those items out of that shed. Those items included pantyhose, underwear, and a cylinder tube containing lots of jewelry. I do know also that there is a park behind his house with a ditch that runs through it. &#40;I used to play in it&#41; Someone that lives behind him took that shot for CNN!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9895-->
<!--Post: 9899--><!--Time: 1109697074-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9899"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ozdude<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ozdude<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 9:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky, I saw it locally on KSN, too. Hope the media and rubber-neckers show a little respect for your family and their property.  <BR> <BR>I&#39;d also like to point out that, to me, it was inappropriate for that investigator to be pulling that stuff out in plain view where someone with a camera could catch it. I&#39;d also like to point out his clothing was labeled FBI. Speaking of, there has been a lot of WPD bashing, but what about the other assisting agencies. They apparently had nothing of value to add in 31 years, did they? Why not bash them, too?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9899-->
<!--Post: 9906--><!--Time: 1109699478-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9906"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 9:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Oz - cute name by name, you should here people make fun of me when I tell them where I&#39;m from! Bet they don&#39;t anymore! HA! No, they are not respecting they opened up the area this morning! The on lookers are abundant! What do they think they&#39;ll see? Anyway, that shot came from someone/media across the park and behind Rader&#39;s house. We saw a media antenna up over there. It was not in plan view, they really had a powerful lense to get that shot. I&#39;m wondering why, investigators didn&#39;t have a blanket over that shed? They parked their crime scene trucks in front of the house at an angle where media couldn&#39;t see what they were taking to it!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9906-->
