<!--Post: 10243--><!--Time: 1109837580-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10243"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stormy74<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stormy74<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 12:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Oooh Foxfire...&#42;shakes head at that post&#42; haha. Yes, I also noticed the Christmas lights, but there is something else about the pictures I have seen that bothers me. For someone who is so supposedly meticulous the place looks cluttered to me. Again, though, Bestbud made a valid point about the weather. I guess DR could have been too busy writing, posting, etc. as well...Ok, that was almost as bad as the &#39;brick&#39; thing! lol<!--/Text--></td></tr>
