<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10382"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:blingbling1169@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Cawichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cawichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 10:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Okay guys! Back to what&#39;s in the back yard! What do you think is back there besides the already mentioned s&#42;&#42;&#42; for grass, a table w/ a brick, a serial killer book, some panty hose, a necklace or 2 and a crappy looking &#34;shed&#34;. Gosh, now that you mention it, why didn&#39;t they cite his ass or talk to the city about the fact that his house aint the epitomy of clean and the guy keeps his lights up? I mean, if a guy was rude and nosey, shot a dog in front of me and my kids, was taking pictures of the back of my house when he didn&#39;t need to, was measuring the grass and was generally mean, why not ask for someone else to pick up the stray animals? I mean, how hard is that? C&#39;mon Kansas, we can do better than that! He was a harraser and a weirdo and here in Cali, we would have got rid of him a long time ago. People who can perform menial jobs aren&#39;t hard to find. Has anyone heard of them digging in the back yard or are they only going to focus on the shed? It seems to me if there was really something in the back yard worth retreiving we would have at least heard they were digging, right? You can&#39;t hide piece of construction equiptment from Larry Hatteburg, can you? One more thing, are they going to persue a charge of attempted murder for Kevin Bright? It&#39;s only right and fair for him as well. Maybe they just haven&#39;t mentioned it. I know they haven&#39;t mentioned a lot of the charges he has to be facing like breaking and entering, robbery, theft, grand theft auto, criminal threats, eluding and evading and many others, huh?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10382-->
<!--Post: 10389--><!--Time: 1109918948-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10389"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 10:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I hope they find something more up to date because the nut was Working for the US Census Bureau in 1989 and running around measuring peoples flipping grass, Remeber when he said he had ways to release his whatever? what was that exactly, and beinga control freak, why the Christmas lights, everything else in his life was controled, or Dennis lived in the house and Denny the nut hung outside in the shed and forgot to tell the other personality to take down the Lights,\E.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10389-->
