<!--Post: 10508--><!--Time: 1109977201-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10508"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 3:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ember, <BR> <BR>I owe you an “on topic” post. <BR> <BR>What&#39;s buried in Rader&#39;s back yard?... <BR> <BR>Survey Says!… human remains. <BR> <BR>Hating the thought of it – but – there are so many unsolved HOMO-cides and disappearances. <BR> <BR>I have these reasons to believe it is so: <BR> <BR> <BR>Control <BR> <BR>No consecration <BR> <BR>No crime scene <BR> <BR>Copycat <BR> <BR>Relics/ Souvenirs <BR> <BR>Infinite torture for the victim’s survivors <BR> <BR>He is a homocidal maniac <BR> <BR> <BR>I know this is not easy to talk about. In fact this is all I want to say about it myself. <BR> <BR>Discuss, if you have the stomach. <BR> <BR>LDog  <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10508-->
<!--Post: 10514--><!--Time: 1109979467-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10514"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ozdude<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ozdude<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 3:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->KAKE &#40;here we go again with KAKE&#41; reported at 5pm that &#34;sources in law enforcement&#34; said jewelry was found that doesn&#39;t belong to any of the known 10 victims. If this was posted already somewhere else, too bad. I have Fred Flintstone dial up technology and it takes too long to do a lot of searching.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10514-->
<!--Post: 10518--><!--Time: 1109981137-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10518"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lctrip<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lctrip<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 4:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->LDog you&#39;ve always got something good to contribute, but this time I&#39;m not so sure I agree with you.  Yes there&#39;s lots of unsolved murders, but while I think Denny gets off on reliving his &#39;moments of glory&#39; &#40;glory for him, horrific for us&#41;, I just don&#39;t think he would be the type to keep human remains that close.  First off, it would be tough to bury properly &#40;ya gotta go deep&#41; because if you don&#39;t the dogs will find them.  Secondly, they decompose so eventually there wouldn&#39;t be too much to look at which leads to my final thought which is it strikes me as being too &#39;dirty&#39; for his neat and tidy tastes. <BR> <BR>Sure hope I&#39;m right on this one because that would take this horror to an even lower level than it&#39;s already at. <BR> <BR>Besides, aren&#39;t there recovered bodies for most &#40;all?&#41; of the unsolved murders on the possible BTK victims?  Haven&#39;t read every one but I can&#39;t recall one where there wasn&#39;t. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10518-->
<!--Post: 10519--><!--Time: 1109981522-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10519"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 4:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->we have been working on the Rader timeline, vicims link, have been noticing some really strange things, some of the vics. are probably his, that have that MO and some about 7 to date are not but they to have the same Mo, I would not be suprised at this point to find bodies in his back yard, or planted in the flower bed at a relatives house, He did list Gardening a a hobby, I know not funny<!--/Text--></td></tr>
