<!--Post: 11752--><!--Time: 1111112836-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11752"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Megabyte<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Megabyte<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 17, 2005 - 6:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Does anybody know if investigaters of recovered Joe Otero&#39;s watch and the Nancy Fox Necklace?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11752-->
<!--Post: 11754--><!--Time: 1111116884-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11754"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 17, 2005 - 7:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Meg - I don&#39;t think anything has been disclosed by LE with regards to what they found in DTDC home or shed. Some of us did see a CNN shot of them pulling items out of the shed and those items included: <BR>pantyhose <BR>a white cylinder tube full of jewlery <BR>women&#39;s underwear <BR>a book about serial killers <BR>So, I guess well know soon if Mr. Otero&#39;s watch and Ms. Foxs&#39; necklace is among those items.  <BR> <BR>I can tell you as well, that I knew if they found anything related to Marine Hedge or Mrs. Davis in that shed we would know the next day at the press conference that they were going to charge DTDC for their murders as well, and in fact they did.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11754-->
<!--Post: 11756--><!--Time: 1111120008-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11756"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 17, 2005 - 8:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->KSN TV reported on February 28th that a computer, a printer and a plastic container were removed from Dennis Rader&#39;s house. Removed from his shed were a pair of black pantyhose in a plastic bag, a yellow hard hat, jewelry stored in a cylinder and book titled &#39;100 Most Famous Criminals.&#39; <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.ksn.com/news/stories/7045823.html" target=_top>http://www.ksn.com/news/stories/7045823.html</a> <BR> <BR>It&#39;s interesting that investigators were interested in that yellow hard hat. It begs the question did Rader pose as a construction worker in a murder? <BR>I also remember reading somewhere that none of the jewelry found in the cylinder recovered from Rader&#39;s shed matched any of the 10 murders that he is charged with. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11756-->
<!--Post: 11778--><!--Time: 1111164169-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11778"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sidewalker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sidewalker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 18, 2005 - 8:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->After looking again at the picture of the &#42;shed&#42; I do not see any christmas lights. It looks like wiring, maybe telephone? or electrical? <BR>I dont think I either see Christmas lights or am not looking in the right place.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11778-->
<!--Post: 11787--><!--Time: 1111175136-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11787"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Surfietx<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Surfietx<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 18, 2005 - 11:45 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wonder if he was a cross dresser?  You know, like Buffalo Bill in Silence of the Lambs? <BR> <BR>&#34;It rubs the lotion on its skin. It does this whenever it is told.  It rubs the lotion on its skin or else it gets the hose again.&#34; <BR> <BR>Eeewwww!!! <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11787-->
<!--Post: 11806--><!--Time: 1111200463-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11806"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 18, 2005 - 6:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sidewalker, look at the front of the house. <BR><a href="http://www.sfgate.com/cgi-bin/object/article?f=/c/a/2005/03/06/MNGE2BL7CJ1.DTL&amp;o=O" target=_top>http://www.sfgate.com/cgi-bin/object/article?f=/c/ a/2005/03/06/MNGE2BL7CJ1.DTL&amp;o=O</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
